## QUA 2.0 migration

When updating QUA programs or configs for **qm-qua 2.0 / QOP 4**, follow
[docs/plans/qua-2.0-migration.md](../../docs/plans/qua-2.0-migration.md).

Apply migration-guide recipes **literally** when before-patterns match; do not invent variants.

### Breaking-change checklist

| Area | QUA 1 | QUA 2 |
|------|-------|-------|
| Mixers | top-level `mixers`, `mixer`/`lo_frequency` on elements | `imbalance_correction` on `mix_inputs`; `job.set_element_correction()` |
| Element I/O keys | `singleInput`, `mixInputs`, `outputs` | `single_input`, `mix_inputs`, `single_output` / `mix_outputs` |
| Measure/demod | `element_output`, `out1`/`out2`, 5-arg `dual_demod` | ADC from element config; 3-arg `dual_demod`; `"I"`/`"Q"` |
| Sliced demod params | `samples_per_chunk`, `chunks_per_window` | `samples_per_slice`, `slices_per_window` |
| Program structure | single `with program():` body | factor experimental runs into `@shot` methods |
| Runtime mixer API | `qm.set_mixer_correction()` | removed — use `job.set_element_correction()` or rebuild config |

Additional 2.0 changes (see CHANGELOG `[2.0.0]`):
- `digital_marker` → `digital_waveform`
- `reset_phase()` removed → `reset_phase=True` on `play()` / `measure()`
- `for_(lower, upper, step)` — all bounds must be QUA int/fixed; iteration via `with for_() as i`
- `smearing` / `time_of_flight` moved from element to **port** config

### Prior 1.3.1 work (already applied)

Stream and iterable migrations from **qm-qua 1.3.1** are largely done in this repo. See
[docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration.md](../../docs/plans/qua-1.4.0-migration.md) for history.
Use `declare_output_stream()` (not `declare_stream()`), iterables, and `declare_with_stream` for sweep experiments.

### Emulator-based validation (QUA 2 branch)

qm-qua 2.0 has no OPX simulator — only `qua_emulator.QuaEmulator.emulate()`. The validation harness supports it via `--migrated-backend emulate` on [scripts/validate_simulation_baseline.py](../../scripts/validate_simulation_baseline.py) (new [scripts/emulate_waveform_runner.py](../../scripts/emulate_waveform_runner.py)); baseline (`../qua-libs`) is unchanged. Comparison is pulse-schedule structure only (no ADC/measurement modeling). See [VALIDATION.md § QUA 2 branch](../../VALIDATION.md#qua-2-branch-emulator-based-validation-experimental) for full details.

Confirmed blockers for running real (not-yet-migrated) QCA scripts through the emulator, reported as a distinct `BLOCKED` status rather than a crash:
- Script imports QUA 1.4.0-only APIs (`qm.qua.extensions.QuaIterable`, ...) or uses old call signatures (4-arg `for_`) — not present/valid in qm-qua 2.0.
- Config still uses QUA 1.4.0 keys (pulse-level `waveforms` / `digital_marker` / `integration_weights`, element-level `smearing` / `time_of_flight`) — raises `qm.exceptions.ConfigValidationException`.
- Real-time ops (`play`, `measure`, `wait`, `align`, ...) used outside a `@shot` — raises `InvalidStatementContextError`.

Offline smoke test (no real QCA script, no CS rack needed): [tests/test_qua2_emulate_smoke.py](../../tests/test_qua2_emulate_smoke.py) against fixture [tests/fixtures/qua2_emulate_smoke_program.py](../../tests/fixtures/qua2_emulate_smoke_program.py); CI job `qua2-emulate-smoke`.

## Local wheel bundle

QUA 2 and the QUA emulator are **not on public PyPI**. This repo installs them from wheels in [`qua-emulator-0.2.13-delivery/`](../../qua-emulator-0.2.13-delivery/):

- `qm-qua==2.0.0.dev5` — `qm_qua-2.0.0.dev5-py3-none-any.whl`
- `qua-emulator==0.2.13` — `qua_emulator-0.2.13-py3-none-any.whl`

```toml
# pyproject.toml (workspace root)
dependencies = ["qm-qua==2.0.0.dev5", "qua-emulator==0.2.13", ...]

[tool.uv.sources]
qm-qua = { path = "qua-emulator-0.2.13-delivery/qm_qua-2.0.0.dev5-py3-none-any.whl" }
qua-emulator = { path = "qua-emulator-0.2.13-delivery/qua_emulator-0.2.13-py3-none-any.whl" }
```

The tutorial project (`Tutorials/intro-to-QUAlibrate/`) is standalone — use path prefix `../../qua-emulator-0.2.13-delivery/` and run `uv sync` from that directory.

Wheel metadata may declare Python `<3.14` (qm-qua) or `<3.12` (qua-emulator); see the delivery README for tested Python versions.
